loads, the groups API omits injected active alert groups; 25 of 256 samples missing and 13 of 20 reload-return samples missing.","causal_explanation":"Reload callback stops the old dispatcher and starts a replacement dispatcher with empty aggrGroupsPerRoute; Groups and the groups API serve the replacement before active groups are rebuilt.","causal_status":"SUPPORTED","evidence_refs":["OBS1","OBS3","SRC-CU-647de303c8be8ecb","SRC-CU-HELPER-c76cc3560e30e77d","SRC-CU-HELPER-bc10f713a675d94d"],"id":"V1","relation_id":"R4","support_basis":"OBSERVED_AND_STATIC"}}],"extension_gaps":[{"id":"GAP-1","locator_hint":{"path":"dispatch/dispatch.go","symbol":"Dispatcher"},"summary":"Full Dispatcher and aggrGroup definitions are needed to determine ownership, per-group context/cancel and timer lifetime, which govern whether aggregation state can be seeded into or carried over by a replacement dispatcher."},{"id":"GAP-2","locator_hint":{"path":"dispatch/dispatch.go","symbol":"processAlert"},"summary":"Agrregation-group rebuild path (processAlert/runAG/doMaintenance) is needed to know when a replacement dispatcher's aggrGroupsPerRoute is repopulated and whether a readiness signal can be derived."},{"id":"GAP-3","locator_hint":{"path":"provider/mem/mem.go","symbol":"Subscribe"},"summary":"Mem provider subscription semantics are needed to know whether a new dispatcher subscriber synchronously receives the current active alerts or only asynchronously, which determines whether a synchronous rebuild is possible."},{"id":"GAP-4","locator_hint":{"path":"dispatch/dispatch.go","symbol":"Stop"},"summary":"Dispatcher.Stop and Run completion semantics are needed to know whether the old dispatcher is fully torn down and whether its aggregation state is still usable by a replacement."}],"instruction":"Prior claims are not trusted facts or edit permission. Cite only exact current evidence_catalog records; unavailable IDs cannot support claims. Reassess the listed gaps and prior static inference. Missing final/live observation limits verification, not source-supported fault inference. Revise or withdraw claims when current evidence warrants it; explain in causal_explanation/evidence_gaps.summary. Missing repair helpers may be introduced only with evidenced caller/interface prerequisites and edit permission. Unobserved outcomes remain UNKNOWN. Do not automatically retain old verdicts.","omitted_claim_count":0,"prior_diagnosis_digest":"d5cc1cfe3652519dc49bb5f35cf897d7820aa0cd0bdaa28789c61fc18cfea26b","snapshot_id":"007325c7f55977c4afd2dfae9e3213373126ad9d11f0854be1d3f54f8fe89308"},"evidence_catalog":[{"content_digest":"ed88ef18ac6f40dd7cebfde50d4c340bcf2fdf1d0ccaefcef6c1425cbaa7ed1d","excerpt":"func (d *Dispatcher) run(it provider.AlertIterator) {
	maintenance := time.NewTicker(d.maintenanceInterval)
	defer maintenance.Stop()

	defer it.Close()

	for {
		select {
		case alert, ok := <-it.Next():
			if !ok {
				// Iterator exhausted for some reason.
				if err := it.Err(); err != nil {
					d.logger.Error("Error on alert update", "err", err)
				}
				return
			}

			d.logger.Debug("Received alert", "alert", alert)

			// Log errors but keep trying.
			if err := it.Err(); err != nil {
				d.logger.Error("Error on alert update", "err", err)
				continue
			}

			now := time.Now()
			for _, r := range d.route.Match(alert.Labels) {
				d.processAlert(alert, r)
			}
			d.metrics.processingDuration.Observe(time.Since(now).Seconds())

		case <-d.startTimer.C:
			if d.state == DispatcherStateWaitingToStart {
				d.state = DispatcherStateRunning
				d.logger.Debug("started", "state", "running")
				d.logger.Debug("Starting all existing aggregation groups")
				for _, groups := range d.aggrGroupsPerRoute {
					for _, ag := range groups {
						d.runAG(ag)
					}
				}
			}

		case <-maintenance.C:
			d.doMaintenance()
		case <-d.ctx.Done():
			return
		}
	}
}
